  "title": "SparrKULee: A Speech-Evoked Auditory Response Repository from KU Leuven, Containing the EEG of 85 Participants",
  "description": "SparrKULee is a speech-evoked auditory response repository from KU Leuven containing EEG recorded with a BioSemi system from normal-hearing native Dutch/Flemish speakers listening to continuous speech (short stories and varying stories) and resting-state sessions. This NEMAR re-host contains 80 of the original 85 participants, as five subjects' raw files are access-restricted at the source repository. The dataset supports research on neural tracking of speech and auditory EEG modelling.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BioSemi ActiveTwo system (BDF format) while normal-hearing young adults listened to continuous speech stimuli across multiple sessions, plus resting-state recordings. Triggers align recordings with the stimuli; a few recordings have missing triggers.",
  "license": "Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC 4.0) for the EEG data. Stimuli can only be used for non-commercial purposes.",
